-- `trade` controlled vocabulary for Cloudflare D1 (AECI-538 epic / AECI-540).
-- Canonical seed + source of truth for the main-app `taxonomy_trades` table, mirroring
-- apps/api/seed/data-objects.sql. Materialises the closed 34-term vocabulary from
-- docs/TRADES_VOCABULARY.md (§5) / its generated mirror docs/trades-vocabulary.json.
--
-- Idempotent UPSERTs keyed on slug; ids are deterministic UUIDv5(slug) so they are stable
-- across re-runs and environments. Applied with `pnpm db:seed:trades:local` →
-- `wrangler d1 execute aeci-app-<env> --file=seed/trades.sql` (and the per-env --remote
-- seed step in scripts/d1-apply-migrations.sh). NEVER deletes — a delete would cascade to
-- product_trades. Writes taxonomy_trades ONLY; product_trades rows come from the promote
-- flow (AECI-542), never from this seed (ADR 0008).
--
-- `description` is seeded NON-NULL for every term (the column is `not null`): /trades/:slug
-- ships as an SEO landing page, so copy is part of the contract. `aliases` is a JSON array,
-- dual-purpose (TRADES_VOCABULARY.md §4): the promote ingest resolves an incoming trade
-- find-only by slug → name → alias (never find-or-create), AND AECI-545 indexes the aliases
-- as searchable-only Algolia content so "blacktop"/"glazier" reach the right products.
--
-- UUIDv5 namespace = UUIDv5(URL_NS, 'https://aecintegrations.com/vocabulary/trade')
--                  = af0d33bc-5814-524f-9c6c-cac49b84d5f0
-- (URL_NS = 6ba7b811-9dad-11d1-80b4-00c04fd430c8, RFC 9562 §6.6). Ids are not stored in the
-- doc or the JSON mirror — they are derived from the slug. This is the same construction
-- data-objects.sql uses, one vocabulary path along; `uuidv5(slug, NAMESPACE)` in any RFC
-- 9562 implementation reproduces a row's id. The executable reference is `uuidv5()` in
-- src/test/d1.spec.ts, which re-derives all 34 ids and asserts they match this file.
--
-- Edit the doc table + the JSON mirror, then regenerate this file — never hand-edit rows
-- (the d1.spec drift test asserts every id/name/description/display_order/alias matches).

ON CONFLICT ("slug") DO UPDATE SET
  "name" = excluded."name",
  "description" = excluded."description",
  "display_order" = excluded."display_order",
  "aliases" = excluded."aliases",
  "updated_at" = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%fZ','now');
